<!--
  <sui-accordion-item> — co-located child for <sui-accordion>.
  Native disclosure: a <details>/<summary> pair per item. Open/close,
  keyboard activation, and ARIA expanded-state are the browser's.

  Prop parity vs <ship-accordion-item>
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Lit                          SUI                      Notes
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  value (string, '')           value (string, '',       ✓
                                 reflect)
  disabled (bool, false)       disabled (bool, reflect) ✓ LANG-GAP below
  open (bool, false)           open (bool, reflect)     ✓ managed by parent,
                                                          mirrors <details open>
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  slots: trigger               trigger                  ✓ rendered inside
                                                          <summary>
         (default) content     (default) content        ✓
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  parts: trigger, content,     trigger, content,        ✓
         chevron                chevron
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ARIA: aria-expanded + aria-controls on trigger;   native <details>/<summary>
        role="region" + aria-labelledby on content    semantics — browser-owned,
        region                                        no explicit aria-* set
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  animation: grid-template-rows 0fr→1fr              LANG-GAP — dropped, see
                                                       sui-collapsible's note
                                                       (same underlying gap)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  NATIVE REBUILD (native-rebuild-gate pass)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - The trigger button/content pair becomes a <details>/<summary>. The
    per-item controller no longer manages aria-expanded/aria-controls/
    role/aria-labelledby by hand, and no longer listens for click —
    the browser's native disclosure does all of that.
  - ROUGH EDGE / step back from the prior L1-button dissolve: the
    trigger can no longer BE the framework's L1 `<button ghost>`
    control, because the native toggle affordance must be the
    <summary> element itself (nesting a real <button> inside <summary>
    would create two overlapping focusable/activatable regions — a
    real a11y regression, not a hypothetical one). So `<summary
    class="trigger">` is hand-styled here to visually match the ghost
    button look (hover wash, focus ring, disabled opacity) instead of
    reusing CONTROL_CONTRACTS_CSS. Flagged for the operator: either
    accept the hand-styled summary permanently, or give the framework
    a `<summary>`-shaped L1 control contract later.
  - LANG-GAP: native <details> has no `disabled`. The controller keeps
    a small capture-phase click/keydown listener that blocks toggling
    when the `disabled` prop is set (same pattern as sui-collapsible).
  - LANG-GAP: the grid-rows open/close animation is dropped — same
    underlying reason as sui-collapsible (native show/hide has no
    animatable hook without ::details-content, which isn't
    cross-browser yet). Toggling is instant now.
  - Arrow/Home/End cross-item keyboard navigation and single-vs-
    multiple-open coordination remain genuinely-needed JS in the
    controllers — no native HTML expresses "one details open at a
    time across sibling shadow roots" or "arrow-key focus-move
    between headers".
  - No tone channel on this component — nothing to globalize there.
  - The chevron stays a hand-authored inline <svg> (not the `<icon>`
    language element) — same reasoning as before this pass (color
    swap + rotate, `<icon>` has no tone/color channel yet, a LANG-GAP
    already documented in its own source).
  - `display:block`/`color`/`[hidden]` on :host — framework-owned
    (BASE_CSS).
-->

<component>{
  props: {
    disabled: bool,
    open: bool,
  },
}</component>
<prop name="value" type="string" default="" reflect />

<variants class="trigger">
  [open]: bg:muted
</variants>
<variants class="chevron">
  [open]: fg:foreground
</variants>

<style>
  :host {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
  }

  .trigger {
    display: flex;
    list-style: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    user-select: none;
    -webkit-user-select: none;
    transition: background var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .trigger::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .trigger::marker { content: ''; }
  .trigger:hover { background: var(--hover-bg); }
  .trigger:focus-visible {
    outline: var(--focus-ring);
    outline-offset: var(--focus-ring-offset);
  }
  :host([disabled]) .trigger {
    cursor: not-allowed;
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .chevron {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    transition: transform var(--duration-medium) var(--ease-out);
  }
  :host([open]) .chevron { transform: rotate(180deg); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .chevron { transition: none; } }

  .content-body { padding: var(--space-3) 0; }
</style>

<details bind:this={detailsEl}>
  <summary class="trigger" part="trigger" bind:this={triggerEl}
    sx="w:full py:3 px:4 text:sm weight:semibold">
    <row align="center" justify="between" gap="2" sx="w:full">
      <span class="trigger-label"><slot name="trigger"></slot></span>
      <svg class="chevron" part="chevron" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"
        sx="w:icon-size-md h:icon-size-md fg:muted-foreground">
        <path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4"></path>
      </svg>
    </row>
  </summary>
  <div class="content-wrap" part="content">
    <div class="content-body">
      <slot></slot>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>
